{"subject":"Physiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 26.Previous Year Questions","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Physiology::26.Previous_Year_Questions","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436537840","topic":"PrepLadder · 26.Previous Year Questions","number":1,"stem":"Not seen in decompression sickness?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vision loss"},{"label":"B","text":"Hearing loss"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemodilution"},{"label":"D","text":"Coagulopathy"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Hemodilution","solutionHtml":"98b1248373d3\"&amp;gt;sickness (DCS) is caused by <strong>nitrogen bubble formation</strong> due to rapid ascent from high-pressure environments.\n<li><strong>Vision loss</strong> can occur due to <strong>air <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1c07a1135f1692777187f547678386\">embolism</span> affecting the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"fb7a2c30e416927771972f7df6f8c0\">retinal</span> circulation</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Hearing loss</strong> can result from <strong>inner ear <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5b92d758801692777182d17f9d55bc\">barotrauma</span> or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b774537d0c1692777201dee32072fe\">vestibulocochlear</span> involvement</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Coagulopathy</strong> occurs due to <strong>vascular injury and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ba6b77f29316927771807350f86ce2\">activation</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"42f1e4deb8169277718412c0681a54\">coagulation</span> pathways</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Hemodilution is not seen</strong> in DCS because the condition primarily leads to <strong>dehydration</strong>, not <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a0e40688fa169277719572bdb48c92\">plasma</span> volume expansion.</li>\n\n<p><strong>Pathophysiology of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"46a5e63f281692777185d3f56ea186\">Decompression</span> Sickness</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:438px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>System Affected</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Manifestations</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Neurological</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Vision loss, confusion, vertigo, paralysis</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Otorhinolaryngologic</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Hearing loss, tinnitus, dizziness</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Cardiovascular</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Coagulopathy, gas embolism, shock</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Pulmonary</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Dyspnea, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f8034b340e1692777184abcfab32f3\">chest pain</span> (\"chokes\")</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Vision loss (Option A):</strong> Incorrect because <strong>air <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1c07a1135f1692777187f547678386\">embolism</span> can cause <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"fb7a2c30e416927771972f7df6f8c0\">retinal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a66cd3adaa1692777182e77cb23021\">artery</span> occlusion</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Hearing loss (Option B):</strong> Incorrect because <strong>inner ear <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5b92d758801692777182d17f9d55bc\">barotrauma</span> and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"391d32291016927771932bab695579\">nitrogen</span> bubbles can affect hearing</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Coagulopathy (Option D):</strong> Incorrect because <strong>bubble-induced endothelial damage triggers <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c17961c71692777184ab55a9c4df\">clotting</span> abnormalities</strong>.</p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">GK Pal Comprehensive Textbook of Medical Physiology, 1st Edition, Page 955<br/>Guyton and Hall Textbook of Medical Physiology, 14th Edition, Pages 563, 564</div>","tags":""}]}